Q5:
In Java 17+, which statement is true about Sealed Classes?
Options:
A) They prevent any class from being instantiated
B) They allow any class to use their methods without inheritance
C) They allow a class to restrict which classes can extend or implement it
D) They are used primarily to speed up reflection

Answer: C
C)They allow a class to restrict which classes can extend or implement it
Reason:Sealed classes in Java 17 control inheritance by explicitly specifying permitted subclasses using the permits keyword.
