Q8:What is the "Zombie Child" problem in React-Redux or similar state libraries?
Options:
A) A memory leak caused by components not being unmounted properly
B) A component that continues using stale props or state because subscriptions were not cleaned up correctly
C) A component that renders twice in development mode
D) A Redux thunk that never resolves asynchronously

Answer: B
B) A component that continues using stale props or state because subscriptions were not cleaned up correctly
Reason:
The "Zombie Child" problem happens when a component continues receiving outdated store updates due to stale subscriptions or improper cleanup/order of updates.
