Q10:
When using Spring Cloud Config, what is the primary benefit of using a "Bus Refresh" over an /actuator/refresh?

Options:
A) It encrypts configuration values
B) It refreshes configuration across all connected services automatically
C) It stores refreshed configs in memory cache
D) It forces the JVM to reload application classes

Answer: B
B) It refreshes configuration across all connected services automatically
Reason:
Spring Cloud Bus propagates refresh events to all connected microservices, avoiding manual refresh calls on each instance.

